    {
      "type": "tweet",
      "id": "1979864611462738368",
      "url": "https://x.com/dost_pagasa/status/1979864611462738368",
      "twitterUrl": "https://twitter.com/dost_pagasa/status/1979864611462738368",
      "text": "Heavy Rainfall Warning No. 7-A #NCR_PRSD\nWeather System: Tropical Storm RAMIL\nIssued at: 6:40 PM, 19 October 2025(Sunday)\n\nORANGE WARNING LEVEL: Zambales(Iba, Palauig, Candelaria, Masinloc, Santa Cruz).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING is THREATENING.\n\nYELLOW WARNING LEVEL: Bataan, Zambales(Olongapo, Subic, San Marcelino, Cabangan, Castillejos, San Antonio, San Felipe, San Narciso, Botolan), Nueva Ecija(Carranglan, Pantabangan, Bongabon, Lupao), Pampanga(Lubao, Floridablanca, Porac), Tarlac(Bamban, Capas, Mayantoc, San Jose, San Clemente, Camiling), Batangas(Nasugbu, Lian, Tuy, Balayan, Calatagan, Calaca) and Cavite(Maragondon, Ternate, Naic, General Emilio Aguinaldo, Magallanes, Alfonso).\nASSOCIATED HAZARD: FLOODING in flood-prone areas.\nMeanwhile, light to moderate with occasional heavy rains affecting Bulacan, Metro Manila, Quezon, Rizal, Laguna, Nueva Ecija(Cabiao, Gapan, General Tinio, San Antonio, San Isidro, Aliaga, Cabanatuan, Cuyapo, Gabaldon, General Mamerto Natividad, Guimba, Jaen, Laur, Licab, Llanera, Nampicuan, Palayan, Penaranda, Quezon, Rizal, San Jose, San Leonardo, Santa Rosa, Santo Domingo, Munoz, Talavera, Talugtug, Zaragoza), Tarlac(Concepcion, Anao, Tarlac City, Gerona, La Paz, Paniqui, Pura, Ramos, San Manuel, Victoria, Moncada, Santa Ignacia), Pampanga(Sasmuan, Apalit, Arayat, Bacolor, Candaba, San Fernando, Macabebe, Magalang, Masantol, Mexico, Minalin, San Luis, San Simon, Santa Ana, Santo Tomas, Angeles, Mabalacat, Guagua, Santa Rita), Cavite(Amadeo, General Trias, Indang, Mendez, Silang, Tagaytay, Trece Martires, Bacoor, Carmona, Cavite City, Dasmarinas, Gen. Mariano Alvarez, Imus, Kawit, Noveleta, Rosario, Tanza) and Batangas(Agoncillo, Alitagtag, Balete, Batangas City, Bauan, Tanauan, Cuenca, Ibaan, Laurel, Lemery, Lipa, Lobo, Mabini, Malvar, Mataasnakahoy, Padre Garcia, Rosario, San Jose, San Juan, San Luis, San Nicolas, San Pascual, Santa Teresita, Santo Tomas, Taal, Talisay, Taysan, Tingloy) which may persist within 3 hours.\nThe public and the Disaster Risk Reduction and Management Offices concerned are advised to MONITOR the weather condition and watch for the next warning to be issued at 8:00 PM today.\n\nFor more information and queries, please call telephone numbers 8927-1335 and 8927-2877 or log on to https://t.co/59mTpZJq1n.",
